{
  "_note": [
    "The armour class a hero's sheet shows, and now the one the tracker seats",
    "them at (#153, and the fourth rule under #112).",
    "",
    "The server answered this with 10 + DEX until now, because it was the only",
    "answer available at that layer: characters stores raw scores and an",
    "inventory, and the sheet's number was worked out in the browser and never",
    "sent anywhere. A Barbarian reading 15 was seated at 12 and the DM rolled",
    "against the wrong number all fight — failing toward hits landing that",
    "should have missed, which nobody at the table can detect.",
    "",
    "Go has the rule in internal/http/armor.go, TypeScript in lib/derive.ts, and",
    "both answer these cases.",
    "",
    "sources are the data of the hero's class, subclass, species or background —",
    "whatever grants features. Both engines filter them by level first, so a",
    "feature the hero has not reached yet cannot raise their AC.",
    "",
    "items are inventory rows; only equipped ones count. Light armour adds the",
    "whole DEX modifier, Medium at most 2 of it, Heavy none.",
    "",
    "An unarmoredDefense replaces the unarmoured base and never lowers it. Its",
    "shield flag is a real tri-state: absent means the benefit survives carrying",
    "a shield (the Barbarian's does), false means it does not (the Monk's).",
    "",
    "Magic (#189): an item may carry a `bonus` (+1..+3). Armor adds it after its",
    "category's DEX rule, a shield adds it to its board, and a worn `gear` item",
    "(`wear`: cloak, ring, ...) adds it to the wearer on top of everything. An",
    "item that declares `attunement` contributes the bonus only while its row",
    "is attuned — an unattuned Frost Brand is a well-made sword and no more."
  ],
